# OriginalFiles

`OriginalFiles/` is the user's retail disc dump. Never stage, commit, or distribute it (or `*.iso`, `*.xbe`, `*.bnl`, `*.original` payloads).

## Editing OriginalFiles

Before the first change to any file under `OriginalFiles/`:

1. Copy the untouched file beside itself with a `.original` suffix (`default.xbe` → `default.xbe.original`).
2. List the edit in `docs/ORIGINAL_FILES.md`: path, why, what changed, how to restore.

Do not put that markdown inside `OriginalFiles/`. ISO packing must skip `*.original` (use `tools/xemu/build_iso.ps1`, which stages into `cache/xemu_root/`).

```text
# BAD — mutate the dump with no backup
Copy-Item scene.bnl scene.bnl.bak
# GOOD
if (-not (Test-Path scene.bnl.original)) { Copy-Item scene.bnl scene.bnl.original }
# then document in docs/ORIGINAL_FILES.md
```

xemu is a runtime oracle for reconstructed functions (which BNL opens, which AID is requested). See `docs/XEMU.md`.
